/* What the original's loaders do around "Loading...Please Wait": each
 * case run by the original's small picture loader (6961:00e4) or ECL block
 * loader (3775:0361) in an 8086 emulator, in the Tandy mode, with its DAX
 * record read (169c:088e), flush (1614:045c) and key (1614:025b) replaced
 * by traps serving COKAssets' records and digesting the screen. A case is
 * KIND FILE ANIMATION FIRST ID: pic, sprite or ecl, the ECL file
 * (DS:5782), DS:4b4f, the loads made before ('-' for none, else KIND:ID
 * joined by +) and the record; after those, row 24 gets "Row 24 was here
 * before the load:40 cells" in white and row 23 "Row 23 stays" in yellow. The result lists the
 * screen's FNV-1a digest (its first 10 hex digits, the 32,000 bytes of
 * the Tandy layout) at each record read, flush and key and at the end,
 * then the slot (name and record held, DS:6dee and 6e00; DS:6da3; each
 * frame's pixels and mask, first 8 digits) or the ECL buffer's digest.
 * Generated by the leftovers part's harness (mkdata.py), not part of the
 * repository. */
typedef struct {
    const char *script;
    const char *expect;
} loading_case;

